{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 11 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 11 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\nclass InputHandler {\n    private final BufferedReader reader;\n    private String[] tokens;\n    private int tokenIndex;\n\n    public InputHandler() {\n        reader = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        tokens = new String[0];\n        tokenIndex = 0;\n    }\n\n    private void loadTokens() throws IOException {\n        while (tokenIndex >= tokens.length) {\n            String line = reader.readLine();\n            if (line == null) break;\n            tokens = line.split(\"\\\\s+\");\n            tokenIndex = 0;\n        }\n    }\n\n    public int nextInt() throws IOException {\n        loadTokens();\n        return Integer.parseInt(tokens[tokenIndex++]);\n    }\n\n    public long nextLong() throws IOException {\n        loadTokens();\n        return Long.parseLong(tokens[tokenIndex++]);\n    }\n\n    public double nextDouble() throws IOException {\n        loadTokens();\n        return Double.parseDouble(tokens[tokenIndex++]);\n    }\n\n    public String next() throws IOException {\n        loadTokens();\n        return tokens[tokenIndex++];\n    }\n}\n\npublic class FinalSolution {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {\n        InputHandler handler = new InputHandler();\n        int n = handler.nextInt();\n        int budget = handler.nextInt();\n        int[] numbers = new int[n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            numbers[i] = handler.nextInt();\n        }\n\n        int even = 0, odd = 0;\n        List<Integer> qualifyingDifferences = new ArrayList<>();\n\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            if (i > 0 && even == odd) {\n                qualifyingDifferences.add(Math.abs(numbers[i] - numbers[i - 1]));\n            }\n            if ((numbers[i] % 2) == 0) {\n                even++;\n            } else {\n                odd++;\n            }\n        }\n\n        Collections.sort(qualifyingDifferences);\n        int maxCount = 0;\n        for (int diff : qualifyingDifferences) {\n            if (budget >= diff) {\n                maxCount++;\n                budget -= diff;\n            } else {\n                break;\n            }\n        }\n\n        System.out.println(maxCount);\n    }\n\n    static int gcd(int x, int y) {\n        if (y == 0) return x;\n        return gcd(y, x % y);\n    }\n\n    static int lcm(int x, int y) {\n        return x * (y / gcd(x, y));\n    }\n\n    static int powerMod(int base, int exp, int mod) {\n        if (base == 0) return 0;\n        if (exp == 0) return 1;\n        long res;\n        if ((exp & 1) == 0) {\n            res = powerMod(base, exp >> 1, mod);\n            res = (res * res) % mod;\n        } else {\n            res = base % mod;\n            res = (res * powerMod(base, exp - 1, mod)) % mod;\n        }\n        return (int) ((res + mod) % mod);\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\nfrom typing import List\n\nclass InputHandler:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.reader = sys.stdin\n        self.tokens = []\n        self.token_index = 0\n\n    def load_tokens(self):\n        while self.token_index >= len(self.tokens):\n            line = self.reader.readline()\n            if not line:\n                break\n            self.tokens = line.strip().split()\n            self.token_index = 0\n\n    def next_int(self):\n        self.load_tokens()\n        val = int(self.tokens[self.token_index])\n        self.token_index += 1\n        return val\n\n    def next_long(self):\n        self.load_tokens()\n        val = int(self.tokens[self.token_index])\n        self.token_index += 1\n        return val\n\n    def next_double(self):\n        self.load_tokens()\n        val = float(self.tokens[self.token_index])\n        self.token_index += 1\n        return val\n\n    def next(self):\n        self.load_tokens()\n        val = self.tokens[self.token_index]\n        self.token_index += 1\n        return val\n\n\ndef gcd(x: int, y: int) -> int:\n    if y == 0:\n        return x\n    return gcd(y, x % y)\n\n\ndef lcm(x: int, y: int) -> int:\n    return x * (y // gcd(x, y))\n\n\ndef power_mod(base: int, exp: int, mod: int) -> int:\n    if base == 0:\n        return 0\n    if exp == 0:\n        return 1\n    if (exp & 1) == 0:\n        res = power_mod(base, exp >> 1, mod)\n        res = (res * res) % mod\n    else:\n        res = base % mod\n        res = (res * power_mod(base, exp - 1, mod)) % mod\n    return int((res + mod) % mod)\n\n\ndef main():\n    handler = InputHandler()\n    n = handler.next_int()\n    budget = handler.next_int()\n    numbers = [handler.next_int() for _ in range(n)]\n\n    even = 0\n    odd = 0\n    qualifying_differences = []\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        if i > 0 and even == odd:\n            qualifying_differences.append(abs(numbers[i] - numbers[i - 1]))\n        if numbers[i] % 2 == 0:\n            even += 1\n        else:\n            odd += 1\n\n    qualifying_differences.sort()\n    max_count = 0\n    for diff in qualifying_differences:\n        if budget >= diff:\n            max_count += 1\n            budget -= diff\n        else:\n            break\n\n    print(max_count)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00011884459672728553, -9.536738616588991e-07, 0.0, -0.00012694983161054552, -0.055599503219127655, -0.16024594008922577, -0.3485107123851776, -0.5342388153076172, -5.960462772236497e-07, -5.245195097813848e-06, -0.0034116655588150024, -0.002188075101003051, -5.125986263010418e-06, -9.536738616588991e-07, -7.152531907195225e-06, -1.0371154530730564e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.3589766240329482e-05, -8.344646857949556e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.52720492426306e-05, -1.0132738680113107e-05, -5.364403477869928e-06, -0.00011574551899684593, -9.536697689327411e-06, -0.00018439977429807186, -4.529942543740617e-06, -3.218599158572033e-05, -5.960462772236497e-07, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -6.496695277746767e-05, -0.003601732663810253, -4.887569048150908e-06, -1.7881377516459906e-06, -4.768370445162873e-07, -7.271740287251305e-06, -0.04859050735831261, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -0.28128957748413086, -7.629365427419543e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.014176847413182259, -0.0009147512027993798, 0.0, -0.020547155290842056, -2.264974000354414e-06, -4.029192859889008e-05, -2.264974000354414e-06, -2.3841830625315197e-06, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.50339189733495e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -4.887569048150908e-06, -1.597391747054644e-05, -1.6689286894688848e-06, -5.245195097813848e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -6.437280717364047e-06, -3.9219088648678735e-05, -2.9802276912960224e-06, -0.0021873614750802517, -3.2186455882765586e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.043001510202884674, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.00043335105874575675, -2.145764938177308e-06, -0.02334187924861908, 